Subject: [PATCH] tee: qseecom: wipe application invoke staging before release

Application requests, responses and address-patched auxiliary buffers are
copied into a dedicated TrustZone allocation. These copies may contain
credentials or authentication tokens. Neither releasing a qcom_tzmem chunk
nor destroying its pool guarantees that its contents are cleared.

Explicitly clear the complete allocation at the common cleanup label, after
successful response copy-back and before returning memory to the allocator.
The same cleanup handles failures after any request or auxiliary copy.

diff --git a/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c b/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
index 296e7175588223c66d06c3c90cc5c9d04e5f844c..00ab4eb406e9f97b93016bb302c1cc46e59d2e48 100644
--- a/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
+++ b/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
@@ -982,6 +982,8 @@ static int qseecom_tee_invoke_func(struct tee_context *ctx,
 		}
 
 out_free:
+		/* Clear credentials and other sensitive application data. */
+		memzero_explicit(b, bc.initial_size);
 		qcom_tzmem_free(b);
 		qcom_tzmem_pool_free(bp);
 
